The common difference is \[
\begin{aligned}
d&=\frac{a_5-a_1}{5-1} \\
&=\frac{14-2}{4} \\
&=3
\end{aligned}
\]. Thus \[
\begin{aligned}
a_{10}&=a_1+9d \\
&=2+27 \\
&=29
\end{aligned}
\]. Therefore \[
\begin{aligned}
S_{10}&=\frac{10(a_1+a_{10})}{2} \\
&=5(2+29) \\
&=155
\end{aligned}
\].

Compute the first terms: \(a_1=0\), \(a_2=\frac{1}{2}\), \(a_3=\frac{2}{3}\), \(a_4=\frac{3}{4}\). The pattern is \(a_n=\frac{n-1}{n}\). If \(a_n=\frac{n-1}{n}\), then \[
\begin{aligned}
a_{n+1}&=\frac{1}{2-\frac{n-1}{n}} \\
&=\frac{1}{\frac{n+1}{n}} \\
&=\frac{n}{n+1}
\end{aligned}
\], so the pattern holds by induction. Hence \(a_{2024}=\frac{2023}{2024}\).
